CHRISTOPHER-OPENCLAW-AUTOPILOT.sh
CHRISTOPHER-OPENCLAW-AUTOPILOT-README.md

It includes:

Seven OpenClaw agents: Christopher, Strategist, Researcher, Builder, QA, Browser, and Memory.
OpenClaw ↔ Codex/ChatGPT-style terminal conversations using pipeable codex exec. Official Codex documentation
Claude Code, OpenAI API, and Ollama fallback routes.
OpenClaw’s browser dashboard, isolated browser, ChatGPT webpage route, and official Chrome extension. OpenClaw browser documentation
Persistent mission transcripts, plans, task breakdowns, QA verdicts, and bounded repair loops.
Full OpenClaw/Gateway/browser/model/agent/GPU/Codex/Ollama doctor checks.
Daily systemd continuation mode.
Supported cross-agent sessions and delegation. OpenClaw session tools
Planning agents are technically restricted from host-wide execution.
No autonomous posting, contacting family/friends, spending, deleting data, exposing services, deploying, or pushing to GitHub.

Run on Kubuntu:

chmod +x CHRISTOPHER-OPENCLAW-AUTOPILOT.sh
./CHRISTOPHER-OPENCLAW-AUTOPILOT.sh install --install-missing

Then:

~/AI-PC/christopher/bin/christopher doctor
~/AI-PC/christopher/bin/christopher dashboard

First real conversation:

~/AI-PC/christopher/bin/christopher council \
  "Inspect my projects, decide what will improve Anthony's life most, break it into tasks, and identify the first useful task" \
  --rounds 3

Authorize bounded project work:

~/AI-PC/christopher/bin/christopher mission \
  "Inspect this application, fix the highest-priority verified problem, and test it" \
  --project ~/Projects/mygig \
  --execute

Enable daily continuation:

~/AI-PC/christopher/bin/christopher schedule enable --execute

The script passed Bash syntax checking, embedded Python compilation, clean-install, provider-failure, and doctor smoke tests.
